From 5899d152539a3c44332fa72f06ae2774aaa9cbb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:00:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GUI G2: the desktop application + plain ISO boot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tools/gui_app.py is the native desktop app (tkinter, stdlib only -- no
browser, no third-party packages), in Russian, with two switchable
modes: Normal (machine list, transport buttons, live screen, a
three-step "new machine" wizard with iso/disk/kernel/empty boot media)
and Expert (the full SCHEMA option surface, monitor console,
artifacts, snapshots, TAP responder, run logs).  Both modes share the G1
core (tools/launcher.py Machine/MonitorClient); frame buffers render
through the FB keyframe protocol and the end stop keeps T5 semantics
("Stop" sends quit, the emulator prints stats and writes artifacts).
make gui runs the app, make gui-web keeps the browser GUI; build.bat
gui / build.bat gui-web / gui.bat match on Windows.

"Select an ISO and start" boots it like VirtualBox/VMware: the wizard's
iso kind builds --rom=<bios.bin> --lpc=ich9 --sata=<iso> (the documented
docs/WINDOWS.md §E recipe) and a stock SeaBIOS is located via the
remembered pick, ~/.x86emu-gui, the repo or $AURALITE_BIOS.  The
acceptance lane is tests/test_iso_boot.py over tools/mkiso.py +
tests/fixtures/bootstub.nas: a 1 MiB ISO9660+El Torito+MBR test image
whose stub prints AURA_ISO_BOOT_OK to COM1; lane Q (SATA-as-disk) must
see the marker (measured 8.2 s wall, 120M executed steps on stock
SeaBIOS 1.16.3) and lane C (ATAPI/El Torito) SKIPs until STORE S6.
make test-iso joins make test and make test-sanitize; everything SKIPs
cleanly without nasm or a bios.bin.

Three measured defects fixed along the way.  IDENTIFY DEVICE carried
three un-honest fields: the model was not byte-pair swapped (firmware
displayed "uAariLetE umiDksH AB") and legacy CHS words 1/3/6 were zero,
so stock SeaBIOS reported PCHS=0/0/0, rounded the LCHS translation to
zero cylinders and refused every CHS read with EPARAM -- the small test
image could not boot at all (negative control: reverting the swap turns
the two test_ahci asserts red).  Unknown CLI options were silently
ignored (a --cdrom= typo booted a disk-less machine and looked like a
firmware failure); main.c now refuses them with usage + exit 1, the
same contract as the GUI schema, pinned by an NC in test_iso_boot.py.
The IVT dispatch receipt is now opt-in (AURALITE_IVT_LOG=1): the
unconditional log measured 9381 lines during a stock SeaBIOS keyboard
spin-up alone and dominated BIOS-boot wall time.

Gates (sequential): make test rc=0 (587 ok, 2 expected SKIPs: the CD
lane and the Tk construction lane without a display), make test-sanitize
rc=0 (265 ok), make fuzz (512 programs / 12288 states match), perf bench
ok.  Test hygiene pinned where the gate load measured flakes: the
find_seabios vectors are hermetic against a real $AURALITE_BIOS and the
launcher WS frame wait tolerates 10-20x slower sanitized builds.
